     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Hello,</span><div><font color=\"#222222\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I have two question for using MaAsLin in R.</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">The first,</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">My 16s sequence data need to be normalized.</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#222222\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">MaAsLin document suggest that abundances should be normalized by dividing each abundance measurement by the sum of the column abundances (relative abundance).</font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I think that just dividing by sum is not enough to nomalize my sequence data.</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font color=\"#222222\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I used QIIME for CSS normalization.</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">If I want to use CSS-normalized data in Maaslin, how can I use it?</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">The default Maaslin use values between 0 and 1.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">However, the value of CSS is not between 0 and 1, so I cannot use it in MaAsLin.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Let me know the option for using CSS data in MaAsLin.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">The second,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">For performing MaAsLin, may I normalize my data using CSS method, then divide each sequence count by the total sequence count?</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">In other words, I want this way, 1) raw sequence count data --&gt; 2) CSS normalization using QIIME--&gt; 3) dividing each abundance by the sum --&gt; 4) Upload to MaAsLin --&gt; 5) Analysis</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">I found the answer to my question that it&#39;s fine either CSS or dividing by sum of value, not both.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">I don&#39;t know why I cannot use both CSS and dividing by sum (the first CSS normalization then dividing by sum in CSS normalized data).</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Could you explain why not both?</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Thank you.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Regards,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Hanna</div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\">Han-Na Kim Ph.D<br>Research Professor<br>Ewha Womans Univ., School of Medicine, Seoul, Korea<br></div></div></div></div></div>"
